---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="A viral stream hits the CDN" hint="A new segment appears and every viewer asks for it within a fraction of a second. Choose how the caches are arranged and see who has to answer.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>By default, with <b>1,000 points of presence</b>, <b>coalescing on</b> and <b>no shield</b>, every PoP sends one request per rendition: <b>5,000 requests</b> reach the origin in 150 ms, which is <b>33,333 per second</b> against a capacity of 20,000. Only 60% of the viewers get the segment on time, and 40% are late.</li>
    <li>Turn the <b>Origin shield</b> on: the origin sees <b>5 requests</b> (one per rendition) and the shield takes the 33,333 per second, which it can serve. Nobody is late. Then switch to <b>3,000 PoPs</b> without the shield: 100,000 per second, and 80% of the viewers are late.</li>
    <li>Turn <b>Edges coalesce identical requests</b> off with the shield on: about <b>500,000 requests</b> now reach the shield, one per waiting viewer, and it is overwhelmed at 3.3 million per second. Changing the number of viewers hardly matters while coalescing is on, because the origin's load follows the number of PoPs, not viewers.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg lsb" data-lsb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Viewers on the stream <select class="pg-in" data-v><option value="100000">100,000</option><option value="1000000" selected>1,000,000</option></select></label>
      <label>CDN points of presence <select class="pg-in" data-e><option value="200">200</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option><option value="3000">3,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Segment length <select class="pg-in" data-seg><option value="2" selected>2 seconds</option><option value="6">6 seconds</option></select></label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-coal checked /> Edges coalesce identical requests</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" data-shield /> Origin shield between the edges and the origin</label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Requests leaving the edges</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Load on the shield</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Load on the origin</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Viewers who get the segment late</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 5 renditions watched by 10%, 35%, 30%, 20% and 5% of the viewers, with a random 80% to 120% variation per PoP and rendition. The burst for a new segment lasts 150 ms, which is the time an edge needs to fetch it. Without coalescing, half of an edge's viewers ask before the answer arrives and each of those requests goes upstream. The origin handles 20,000 requests per second, the shield 200,000, and any excess is not served in time. Glass-to-glass latency is 1.2 s plus four segment lengths, which is a hold-back of three segments.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lsb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const W = [10, 35, 30, 20, 5];
    const SEED = 11; const JITTER = { base: 80, span: 41 }; // per-PoP audience is 80%..120% of its even share
    const VIEWERS_PER_REQ = 2; // without coalescing, about one request per two waiting viewers
    const BURST_MS = 150; const MS_PER_S = 1000; // requests for a new segment arrive within 150 ms
    const SHIELD_CAP = 200000; const ORIGIN_CAP = 20000; // requests per second
    const LAT = { baseS: 1.2, segments: 4 }; // glass-to-glass latency: fixed part plus four segments of buffer
    const fmt = (n: number) => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
    function simulate(V: number, E: number, coal: boolean, shield: boolean, seg: number) {
      let seed = SEED; const rnd = (n: number) => { seed = (Math.imul(seed, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0; return (seed >>> 16) % n; };
      let edgeOut = 0;
      for (let e = 0; e < E; e++) for (let r = 0; r < W.length; r++) { const n = Math.floor((((V / E) * W[r]) / 100 * (JITTER.base + rnd(JITTER.span))) / 100); if (n > 0) edgeOut += coal ? 1 : Math.ceil(n / VIEWERS_PER_REQ); }
      const rate = (c: number) => Math.floor((c * MS_PER_S) / BURST_MS);
      const shieldIn = shield ? edgeOut : 0; const originIn = shield ? W.length : edgeOut;
      const sRate = rate(shieldIn); const oRate = rate(originIn);
      const pass = (cap: number, x: number) => (x <= cap ? 100 : Math.floor((cap * 100) / x));
      const pS = shield ? pass(SHIELD_CAP, sRate) : 100; const pO = pass(ORIGIN_CAP, oRate);
      return { edgeOut, shieldIn, sRate, originIn, oRate, pS, pO, late: 100 - Math.floor((pS * pO) / 100), lat: LAT.baseS + LAT.segments * seg };
    }
    function draw() {
      const V = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-v]').value); const E = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-e]').value); const seg = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-seg]').value);
      const coal = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-coal]').checked; const shield = q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-shield]').checked;
      const s = simulate(V, E, coal, shield, seg);
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${fmt(s.edgeOut)} per segment`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = coal ? 'one per rendition and PoP' : 'one per waiting viewer';
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = shield ? `${fmt(s.sRate)} per second` : 'no shield';
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = shield ? (s.pS === 100 ? `within its ${fmt(SHIELD_CAP)} per second` : `over its ${fmt(SHIELD_CAP)} per second, serves ${s.pS}% in time`) : 'edges go straight to the origin';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${fmt(s.oRate)} per second`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${fmt(s.originIn)} requests in ${BURST_MS} ms, capacity ${fmt(ORIGIN_CAP)} per second` + (s.pO < 100 ? `, serves ${s.pO}% in time` : '');
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `${s.late}%`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = `glass-to-glass latency ${s.lat.toFixed(1)} s with ${seg}-second segments`;
      const ok = s.late === 0;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', shield && s.pS < 100 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', s.pO < 100 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', ok ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); out.classList.toggle('bad', !ok);
      out.textContent = ok
        ? (shield ? `Healthy: the shield merges ${fmt(s.shieldIn)} edge requests into ${W.length} for the origin, so the origin's load no longer depends on the audience.` : `Healthy for now: ${fmt(s.originIn)} requests in a burst is within what the origin can serve, but it grows with the number of PoPs. A shield makes it 5.`)
        : (shield ? `Overloaded: without coalescing the edges forward one request per viewer, ${fmt(s.shieldIn)} of them, and the shield cannot absorb ${fmt(s.sRate)} per second. ${s.late}% of viewers are late and will stall.`
          : `Overloaded: ${fmt(s.originIn)} requests hit the origin in ${BURST_MS} ms, ${fmt(s.oRate)} per second against ${fmt(ORIGIN_CAP)}. ${s.late}% of viewers are late and will stall. A shield would reduce this to ${W.length} requests.`);
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
